    "headline": "Verdict by the pre-stated rule: Not supported. The anaemia signal needed DS05 (the independent source) to show a lower haematocrit in young dogs: HL -0.02 L/L (-0.04 to +0.01), which includes 0. DS03 shows it (-0.06, -0.10 to -0.03), but DS03 dogs are S-CB050 dogs and healthy young controls also have a lower haematocrit (check C1). No adult excess of bands or cytokine perturbation. Young dogs presented about one day earlier (DS05, HL -1 day, Cliff's delta -0.23, -0.41 to -0.03; q 0.090).",
    "caveats": [
     "exploratory: S-CB050 and DS05 were seen before this plan.",
     "DS03 natural dogs are S-CB050 dogs (SV-07): one source, not a replication.",
     "Age stands in for prior exposure, breed and size, which are not recorded.",
     "Healthy young dogs have a lower haematocrit than adults, so part of any young-adult difference is normal physiology."
    ]
